title: "LIMEN: Layered Invariant Mediating Epistemic Norms"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Bowe
    given-names: "Jonathan A."
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-05-21"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/jonathan-kellerai/trust-boundary-protocol"
keywords:
  - epistemic boundary layer
  - confidence-gated action
  - cross-domain mediation
  - fail-closed
  - specification
abstract: >-
  Trust Boundary Protocol is a specification for an epistemic boundary layer — a confidence-state
  mediator that lets cooperating systems gate cross-domain actions on a shared
  view of every participant's epistemic readiness. It defines five interfaces,
  shared types, an exception hierarchy, and a set of testable correctness
  constraints, and stops short of implementation.
